WEBVTT

00:03:27.538 --> 00:03:31.704
Landback is about reasserting
Indigenous relationships with the land.

00:03:32.121 --> 00:03:35.871
Relationships that are based on tens
of thousands of years

00:03:35.871 --> 00:03:38.913
of hands-on experience
taking care of our homelands.

00:03:39.913 --> 00:03:42.829
If you've ever tried your hand
at farming or gardening,

00:03:42.871 --> 00:03:47.204
you know that land management takes more
than just showing up with good intentions.

00:03:47.954 --> 00:03:52.288
Globally, Indigenous people are really
good at managing for biodiversity

00:03:52.288 --> 00:03:54.038
and resilient ecosystems.

00:03:54.871 --> 00:03:57.288
That's because we've had
generation upon generation

00:03:57.288 --> 00:04:00.079
to test out what works and what doesn't.